# Module factors of the binary exterior parabolics

The strict invariant filtration 0 < V₁ < V₇ < V is a chief series for the
literal exterior stabilizer of V₁: all three actual induced factors are
irreducible. Mixed wedge coordinates identify the middle factor with the
tensor product of the natural two- and three-dimensional block modules;
complementary-wedge coordinates identify the last factor with the dual of
the natural lower SL₃ block module.

The natural-module comparisons on V₃, V₄ and V/V₆ are actual linear and
representation equivalences for their exterior stabilizers. On V₃, the actor
is explicitly twisted by inverse transpose. The quotient V/V₆ is also
equivariantly isomorphic to the literal shear subgroup under conjugation.
The separate source assembly transports these block actions through its
Levi/residual quotients and identifies the shear subgroup with R̄₆.

Reference: Aschbacher–Smith, Lemma 12.5.2, printed p.817/PDF p.834.
-/
